    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate leaning heavily into our speed-focused strategy, prioritizing high-efficiency matchups to maintain our grip on stolen bases. Our strongest play is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.33), who benefits from an optimal leadoff spot and a significant +14% platoon edge against Cavalli. Similarly, **Caleb Durbin** (68.14) is locked into the utility spot; despite facing a legendary arm in Scherzer, the 5.10 xERA suggests a prime opportunity for **Caleb Durbin** to exploit a favorable matchup, with his aggressive base-running profile providing a high floor regardless of the outcome. **Chase Meidroth** (66.48) also provides excellent value at 2B, as his leadoff status and the +19% SP skill boost from facing Abbott make him a must-start despite the left-on-left dynamic.\n\nWhile our lineup is deep, the most difficult decision involved **Colt Keith**, who narrowly missed the cut. Despite his strong base projection, the combination of a negative L/L platoon split against Messick and his currently projected #5 order position rendered him a bench option behind the higher-upside profiles of **Dillon Dingler** and **Jacob Gonzalez**. We are also keeping a close eye on the rain risk (44%) looming over the stadium hosting **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**. While **Trea Turner** remains a elite play (62.87) due to his speed profile, we must monitor potential rain delays that could impact his aggressive SB game plan. Finally, while **Gary Sanchez** (49.99) and **Pedro Ramirez** (41.74) are on the lower end of our starting thresholds, they remain active to protect our cumulative game caps; our roster depth remains anchored by the fact that core bats like **Yordan Alvarez**, **Junior Caminero**, and **Lars Nootbaar** are off today, allowing us to cycle through specialists like **Christian Yelich** (64.13) to maximize our efficiency.",
